# 3. Important Schema Constraint

The live content structure is the source of truth for this validator.

The validator must **not** use the older simplified `content/TEMPLATE.mdx` schema as the implementation contract if it differs from the live modules.

The live Foundation frontmatter currently includes concepts such as:

```yaml
title:
slug:
module:
level:
description:
readingTime:
labTime:
tools:
  - name:
    type:
    url:
    enterpriseToolsNote:
    cabinetArtifact:
      name:
      description:
      unlocksOn:
      previousModule:
      nextModule:
```

OT modules additionally include role/path metadata such as:

```yaml
roleSlug:
pathSlug:
```

The implementation should inspect the actual repository files and existing TypeScript types/loaders before hard-coding assumptions.

